# Protection gained after blockers are declared doesn't remove a blocker already blocking (CR 702.16f applies only as blocks
# are declared, 509.1b): Bot1's Hired Blade attacks and Bot2 blocks it with Embereth Shieldbreaker (red, 2/1). In the declare
# blockers step Bot1's Mother of Runes gives the Blade protection from red: the Blade stays blocked, so Bot2 takes nothing
# (CR 509.1h, 510.1c), the Shieldbreaker's 2 damage to it is prevented (CR 702.16e, 615), and the Blade's 3 kills the
# Shieldbreaker.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mother of Runes
Hired Blade
Mox Ruby
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Embereth Shieldbreaker
Island x15

